  "hypothesis": "Magnetic Marker Restoration: oriented cross-fault displaced-template correlation and depth-attenuation asymmetry (MMRX-16) stacked on the BPWD PoE base",
  "mechanism": "From a joint RTP+gravity structure tensor, take local strike t and cross-strike normal n (n signed toward increasing depth_to_base_surf, i.e. into the hanging-wall basin). Sample high-pass RTP in strips at -4n (footwall) and +4n + s*t (hanging wall) for s in {-4,-2,0,2,4} px, plus a sigma=1.5 low-passed hanging-wall strip (burial attenuation). Local (sigma=3 px Gaussian window) correlations corr_s measure whether a displacement restores marker continuity across the candidate boundary: restoration gain = max_s corr_s - corr_0. Cross-strike strip-variance ratio measures hanging-wall short-wavelength attenuation from deeper magnetic basement. The same geometry at s in {-4,0,4} on high-pass isostatic gravity gives a second-field restoration gain; min(gain_rtp, gain_grav) requires both fields to restore. A step-without-gain channel explicitly encodes the unfaulted-contact mimic. Sixteen zero-catalogue channels (src/gems88/mmrx.py) are added to the proven PHYS-44 + HGVC-20 + PSGV-20 + VIS-23 base with dual-expectation (cell + 300 m kernel-credit) LightGBM/HGB specialists and the shared Dinkelbach emitter. No catalogue reads inside channel construction.",
  "named_non_fault_mimic": "Unfaulted lithologic/intrusive contact or depositional pinch-out: coincident RTP+gravity step with no displaced-marker restoration gain (encoded as mmrx_mimic_contact); GeoDAWN flight-line levelling seams: rectilinear apparent offsets along survey lines without gravity restoration or basement-depth step; Reversely magnetized volcanic flow margins: strong RTP texture steps with no cross-strike depth attenuation ordering",
